From: CEB-GNRD maintainers <bmc@example.com>
Subject: [PATCH] state: recognize orderly software reboots performed by watchdog

Use the existing board clean-shutdown decision to distinguish orderly
software reboots from unexpected watchdog resets. POR detection and
unexpected-reset SEL logging remain intact. A volatile receipt preserves
the decision if the BMC state daemon restarts within the same boot.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [CEB-GNRD integration]
---

--- a/bmc_state_manager.cpp
+++ b/bmc_state_manager.cpp
@@ -18,6 +18,7 @@
 #include <filesystem>
 #include <fstream>
 #include <iostream>
+#include <system_error>
 
 namespace phosphor::state::manager
 {
@@ -356,8 +357,27 @@
             this->lastRebootCause(RebootCause::Software);
             return;
         case WDIOF_CARDRESET:
-            this->lastRebootCause(RebootCause::Watchdog);
+        {
+            // ASPEED also uses the watchdog for an orderly software reboot.
+            // The health service publishes its decision in /run before
+            // consuming the clean-shutdown marker. Prefer that receipt so
+            // restarting this daemon cannot reinterpret the previous boot.
+            // Read the marker first, then the receipt: publication happens
+            // before marker removal, avoiding a gap between the two reads.
+            std::error_code ec;
+            bool cleanShutdown = std::filesystem::exists(
+                                     "/var/lib/ceb-gnrd/clean-shutdown", ec) &&
+                                 !ec;
+            std::ifstream receipt("/run/ceb-gnrd/previous-clean-shutdown");
+            if (receipt.is_open())
+            {
+                unsigned int clean = 0;
+                cleanShutdown = (receipt >> clean) && clean == 1;
+            }
+            this->lastRebootCause(cleanShutdown ? RebootCause::Software
+                                               : RebootCause::Watchdog);
             return;
+        }
         default:
             this->lastRebootCause(RebootCause::POR);
             // Continue below to see if more details can be found
